layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Smoke Alarm Installation Christchurch | Photoelectric Alarms | Call Now
metaDescription: "Smoke alarm installation across Christchurch by EWRB registered electricians. Photoelectric, interconnected and hardwired alarms fitted from $149, plus rental compliance. Call 0800 120 046."
imgKey: home
faqs:
  - q: "Which smoke alarms do you actually install?"
    a: "Long-life photoelectric alarms with sealed 10-year batteries — the type Fire and Emergency NZ recommends. Photoelectric sensors pick up slow, smoky fires (the kind that start in couches, curtains and overloaded multiboxes) much faster than the old ionisation alarms, and they're far less likely to scream at you for making toast. We also install hardwired 240V alarms and wireless interconnected systems where they fit the house better."
  - q: "Where do smoke alarms have to go in my house?"
    a: "The short version: one in every bedroom, one in the hallway outside the bedrooms, one in the living area, and at least one on every level — including the basement rumpus and the sleepout. For rentals the law is specific: an alarm within 3 metres of each bedroom door and one on each level, minimum. We check the layout on the day and put alarms where they'll actually wake you, not just where it's easy to reach."
  - q: "How much does smoke alarm installation cost in Christchurch?"
    a: "A single photoelectric alarm supplied and fitted is $149. Our most popular job is the whole-home package — three alarms installed for $389, with extra alarms at $119 each. Rental compliance checks are $99. Every price includes GST and the alarm itself, so the number we quote is the number you pay. See our <a href='/pricing/'>pricing page</a> for the full list."
  - q: "Do rental properties have different smoke alarm rules?"
    a: "Yes, and they have teeth. Under the Residential Tenancies Act, landlords must have working smoke alarms within 3 metres of every bedroom doorway and on every level, and any new alarms must be long-life photoelectric or hardwired. Get it wrong and the Tenancy Tribunal can award exemplary damages of up to $7,200. Our <a href='/rental-property-smoke-alarm-compliance/'>rental compliance service</a> sorts the whole thing with a written report for your records."
  - q: "My alarms are hardwired. Can you still replace them?"
    a: "Absolutely — that's exactly the sort of job that needs a registered electrician rather than a stepladder and hope. Hardwired alarms die of old age just like battery ones, and the replacement has to be wired in properly and legally. We swap them for modern 240V photoelectric units with battery backup and issue a Certificate of Compliance for the electrical work."
  - q: "How long does an installation visit take?"
    a: "Most homes are done in under an hour. A three-alarm install is typically 45 minutes; a bigger house with interconnected alarms might take two. We test every alarm before we leave, show you how the hush button works, and take the packaging with us."
